# =====================================================================
#  The house style, as far as it can be stated mechanically.
#
#  Written from the source as it stands rather than adopted from a template:
#  4-space indent, the brace on the same line, `Type* name`, one statement per
#  line where a line has room for one.
#
#  .clang-format is NOT applied to the existing tree, and that is deliberate: a
#  reformat of 48k lines would bury every real change for a long time. It describes
#  what new code looks like, and what a file looks like once it is being edited for
#  another reason anyway.
#
#  SortIncludes is off: the includes in this project carry trailing comments that
#  say why each one is there ("FetchAppIconForTest: the same icon path the media
#  card uses"), and reordering them would detach the note from its include.
# =====================================================================
---
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
Standard: c++20

IndentWidth: 4
TabWidth: 4
UseTab: Never
ColumnLimit: 100

BreakBeforeBraces: Attach
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: Inline
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: false
IndentCaseLabels: true

PointerAlignment: Left
DerivePointerAlignment: false
AlignAfterOpenBracket: Align
AlignTrailingComments: true
SpacesBeforeTrailingComments: 1

NamespaceIndentation: None
SortIncludes: false
FixNamespaceComments: true
MaxEmptyLinesToKeep: 1
